## Problem

Nick is in a live negotiation with a Bowen (QLD) dealer over a 2025 BYD Shark 6 (carsales ad oag-ad-26073354). The salesperson has asked what he realistically wants for his 2014 Passat 118TSI trade-in, and Nick must reply without revealing his floor (~$8k) or contradicting his intended vehicle offer ($50k + government charges, ideally landing at $43k changeover + trade). He has no current market read on whether the Shark 6 listing is a good deal, and no pre-purchase inspection provider lined up in the Bowen region.

## Vision

Nick opens his next dealer conversation holding a coherent single-number strategy: he knows his opening, target, and walk-away, sees that his "$50k" and "$43k + trade" positions are actually the same position expressed two ways, has a ready-to-send reply on the Passat that anchors high without lying, and has an inspection provider he can book the moment a deal is struck. The market data tells him decisively whether to push hard or walk.

## Out of Scope

No contact with the dealer, RACQ, or any provider — information gathering and drafting only (standing directive: collect only, Nick submits). No finance/loan structuring analysis. No re-litigation of the Passat valuation research (prior deep-research report stands: trade $6.5–8.5k, private $10–12.5k). No purchase commitment or deposit action.

## Constraints

- Research runs through the Research skill (CLAUDE.md mandate); bare WebSearch only as disclosed fallback.
- All URLs delivered must be verified live, not recalled from memory.
- Reply drafts in Nick's voice: Australian English, no em dashes, direct peer tone.
- Background-session close: `needs input:` not `result:` (PAI override).

## Goal

Deliver one synthesis that (1) verdicts the $50k+ORC offer against live market data, (2) hands Nick a verbatim Passat reply that anchors near $10k without exposing his $8k floor, (3) reconciles the $50k and $43k+trade positions into one negotiation sequence with named anchor numbers, and (4) lists bookable Bowen-region inspection providers with prices.

